10
00:00:35,983 --> 00:00:39,791
Start with one achievable action. In the habit tracker, choose

11
00:00:39,791 --> 00:00:43,598
New habit. Give it a specific name, such as Read

12
00:00:43,598 --> 00:00:44,359
twenty pages.

13
00:00:46,183 --> 00:00:49,835
Choose a category, select the weekdays you want to repeat,

14
00:00:49,835 --> 00:00:53,486
and pick a color and icon. Choose this month only,

15
00:00:53,486 --> 00:00:56,407
or all existing months. Then select Create habit.

16
00:00:58,217 --> 00:01:02,147
Find your habit row and today’s highlighted column. Click the

17
00:01:02,147 --> 00:01:06,077
scheduled cell to mark it complete. The check appears, and

18
00:01:06,077 --> 00:01:07,649
your progress updates automatically.

19
00:01:09,450 --> 00:01:12,647
You can click again today to undo. Past and future

20
00:01:12,647 --> 00:01:15,844
dates stay locked, and only scheduled days can be checked.

21
00:01:15,844 --> 00:01:18,402
Focus on the action you can take today.

22
00:01:20,217 --> 00:01:23,568
To plan ahead, select the plus beside your month tabs.

23
00:01:23,568 --> 00:01:26,920
Choose the month and year, then Add month. You can

24
00:01:26,920 --> 00:01:29,937
reuse your habits or start a fresh monthly plan.

25
00:01:31,750 --> 00:01:36,206
The dashboard shows completion rate, total check ins, your best

26
00:01:36,206 --> 00:01:40,662
current streak, and active habits. Here, one scheduled action is

27
00:01:40,662 --> 00:01:45,118
complete. The numbers reflect this demonstration, not a promised result.

28
00:01:46,950 --> 00:01:50,550
For focused work, open Pomodoro under Widgets in the desktop

29
00:01:50,550 --> 00:01:54,150
sidebar. Choose the habit you want to work on, then

30
00:01:54,150 --> 00:01:56,310
